title:: Probe - Visuals and Representation Suite
summary:: Comprehensive Guide, Reference, and Embeddable GUI Architecture for the Probe Visualization Suite
categories:: GUI>Visualizers, Diagnostics
related:: Classes/Probe, Classes/ProbeScope, Classes/ProbeSpectrum, Classes/ProbeSpectrogram, Classes/ProbeWaterfall, Classes/ProbeMeter, Classes/ProbeLoudness, Classes/ProbeVectorscope, Classes/ProbeBandAnalyzer, Classes/ProbeSpectralDashboard, Classes/ProbeDashboard, Classes/ProbeInspector, Classes/ProbeHistory, Classes/ProbeTheme

section:: Overview

The strong::Probe - Visuals and Representation Suite:: provides a focused collection of 14 visualizers and measurement instruments for SuperCollider. Each class generates a distinct visual representation of sound and synthesis signals:

definitionList::
## link::Classes/Probe:: || Central suite coordinator and server extension dispatcher (code::s.*Pb::) managing global visualizers and broker telemetry.
## link::Classes/ProbeScope:: || strong::Oscilloscope::: Renders audio waveforms in real time with stationary zero-crossing trigger stabilization, multi-channel track separation, zoom, and hardware-antialiased vector lines.
## link::Classes/ProbeSpectrum:: || strong::FFT Spectrum Analyzer::: Displays real-time frequency distribution across a continuous calibrated dBFS curve with an interactive measurement cursor.
## link::Classes/ProbeSpectrogram:: || strong::2D Sonogram::: Plots a scrolling time–frequency waterfall mapping frequency bands to color intensities.
## link::Classes/ProbeWaterfall:: || strong::2.5D Isometric Stack::: Visualizes evolving spectral history through stacked isometric frequency traces with depth-cued shading.
## link::Classes/ProbeMeter:: || strong::Level Meter::: Displays vertical peak and RMS energy bars with calibrated dB rulers, peak-hold indicators, and multichannel monitoring.
## link::Classes/ProbeLoudness:: || strong::Loudness Meter::: Visualizes ITU-R BS.1770-4 / EBU R128 broadcast loudness (Momentary, Short-Term, Integrated, and Loudness Range).
## link::Classes/ProbeVectorscope:: || strong::Stereo Vectorscope::: Renders stereo sound field distribution as an X/Y Lissajous orbit with Mid/Side polar graticule and phase correlation (-1 to +1).
## link::Classes/ProbeBandAnalyzer:: || strong::ISO 1/3-Octave Analyzer::: Displays a 16-band bar spectrum equipped with exponential lag smoothing to eliminate visual flicker.
## link::Classes/ProbeSpectralDashboard:: || strong::Spectral Workstation::: Consolidates FFT curves, chromagrams, pitch tracking, and spectral descriptors into 4 synchronized presets.
## link::Classes/ProbeDashboard:: || strong::5-Panel Master Console::: Hosts Meter, Scope, Spectrum, Spectrogram, and Loudness simultaneously with global freeze and theme controls.
## link::Classes/ProbeInspector:: || strong::Signal-Flow DAG Inspector::: Renders an interactive topological graph of any SynthDef showing unit generator connections, rate color-coding, and bezier paths.
## link::Classes/ProbeHistory:: || strong::Strip-Chart Recorder::: Logs rolling dynamics over time, plotting peak, RMS, and crest factor dynamics.
## link::Classes/ProbeTheme:: || strong::Theme & Palette Engine::: Coordinates laboratory color schemes (\graphite, \phosphor, \amber, \ice, \puredata) and typography scaling across all running views.
::

note::
For complete details on the underlying dual-tier architecture and internal plumbing, see the Implementation Architecture guide in the project repository.
::

section:: Complete Class Reference & Working Examples

subsection:: 1. Probe (Central Facade & Server Extensions)
link::Classes/Probe:: provides centralized access to all instruments, broker telemetry monitoring, and server extensions:

code::
s.boot;

// 1. Open instruments via server extensions
s.scopePb;
s.meterPb;
s.freqscopePb;
s.dashboardPb;

// 2. Open via class facade
Probe.scope(s, 0, 2);
Probe.spectrum(s, 0);
Probe.loudness(s, 0);

// 3. Inspect shared measurement broker
Probe.broker.inspect;

// 4. Global theme propagation
ProbeTheme.current = ProbeTheme.get(\phosphor);
::

subsection:: 2. ProbeScope (Precision Oscilloscope)
link::Classes/ProbeScope:: offers dual-engine rendering (strong::\smooth:: hardware antialiased vector drawing vs strong::\native:: C++ blit), edge-triggered stationary sync, zoom, and channel layout styles:

code::
(
x = {
    var sig = [SinOsc.ar(150), Saw.ar(75)] * 0.4;
    sig;
}.play;

// Open scope in antialiased smooth mode with tracks style (vertically separated channels)
~scope = ProbeScope(s, 0, 2, theme: \graphite, engine: \smooth, style: \tracks);
)

// Interactive controls via code
~scope.engine = \smooth;      // \smooth or \native
~scope.lineWidth = 2.2;       // adjust vector line stroke width
~scope.fill = true;           // enable translucent ribbon fill
~scope.scopeStyle = \tracks;   // \tracks (separated), \overlay (superimposed), \xy (Lissajous)
~scope.triggerMode = \rising;  // stationary sync: \free, \rising, \falling
~scope.xZoom = 2.0;           // zoom horizontal time axis
~scope.yZoom = 1.5;           // zoom vertical amplitude axis
~scope.toggleFreeze;          // freeze display (pauses synth capture, preserves waveform)
~scope.toggleFreeze;          // unfreeze

x.free;
~scope.close;
::

subsection:: 3. ProbeSpectrum (Unified FFT Spectrum Analyzer)
link::Classes/ProbeSpectrum:: integrates 3 switchable visualization modes (Line curve, 16-Band analyzer, and Spectrogram) with an interactive frequency/dB cursor:

code::
(
x = {
    var mod = SinOsc.ar(120, 0, 300);
    var car = SinOsc.ar(300 + mod) * 0.3;
    var noise = PinkNoise.ar(0.05);
    (car + noise).dup;
}.play;

~spec = ProbeSpectrum(s, 0, fftSize: 2048, theme: \ice);
)

// Switch visualization modes dynamically
~spec.mode = \line;         // High-resolution continuous spectral curve
~spec.mode = \bands;        // 16-band ISO 1/3-octave bar display
~spec.mode = \spectrogram;  // Scrolling time-frequency sonogram

// Toggle linear vs logarithmic frequency axis
~spec.freqMode = 1;         // 1 = Logarithmic (20 Hz - 20 kHz), 0 = Linear

x.free;
~spec.close;
::

subsection:: 4. ProbeSpectrogram (2D Scrolling Sonogram)
link::Classes/ProbeSpectrogram:: provides continuous time-frequency history visualization:

code::
(
x = {
    var sweep = SinOsc.ar(XLine.kr(100, 8000, 6).poll(label: \freq)) * 0.2;
    sweep.dup;
}.play;

~sonogram = ProbeSpectrogram(s, 0, theme: \amber);
)

x.free;
~sonogram.close;
::

subsection:: 5. ProbeWaterfall (2.5D Isometric Spectral Stack)
link::Classes/ProbeWaterfall:: creates an isometric stacked-line waterfall display with depth shading:

code::
(
x = {
    var harm = Mix.fill(8, { |i| SinOsc.ar((i + 1) * 110, 0, 0.1 / (i + 1)) });
    harm.dup;
}.play;

~waterfall = ProbeWaterfall(s, 0, theme: \phosphor);
)

x.free;
~waterfall.close;
::

subsection:: 6. ProbeMeter (Compact Multichannel Peak/RMS Meter)
link::Classes/ProbeMeter:: displays real-time peak, RMS, peak-hold, and a calibrated dBFS scale:

code::
(
x = {
    [Dust2.ar(20) * 0.5, BrownNoise.ar(0.1)];
}.play;

~meter = ProbeMeter(s, numIns: 2, numOuts: 2, theme: \graphite);
)

x.free;
~meter.close;
::

subsection:: 7. ProbeLoudness (ITU-R BS.1770 / EBU R128 Loudness Meter)
link::Classes/ProbeLoudness:: measures broadcast-standard loudness metrics:

code::
(
x = {
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.1, 1.5), Dust.kr(1));
    (PinkNoise.ar(0.2) * env).dup;
}.play;

// Target: \ebu (-23 LUFS) or \streaming (-14 LUFS)
~lufs = ProbeLoudness(s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, target: \streaming);
)

// Query current loudness parameters
~lufs.reset; // reset integrated LUFS measurement
x.free;
~lufs.close;
::

subsection:: 8. ProbeVectorscope (Stereo Lissajous & Phase Correlation)
link::Classes/ProbeVectorscope:: renders stereo field distribution and phase alignment:

code::
(
x = {
    var l = SinOsc.ar(200);
    var r = SinOsc.ar(200, pi * 0.5); // 90 degree phase shift (circular Lissajous)
    [l, r] * 0.2;
}.play;

~vec = ProbeVectorscope(s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, engine: \smooth);
)

~vec.engine = \smooth; // switch between \smooth (vector) and \native
~vec.lineWidth = 2.5;

x.free;
~vec.close;
::

subsection:: 9. ProbeBandAnalyzer (16-Band ISO 1/3-Octave Analyzer)
link::Classes/ProbeBandAnalyzer:: features an adjustable exponential moving-average smoothing filter:

code::
(
x = {
    Saw.ar([100, 200, 400, 800, 1600], 0.1).sum.dup;
}.play;

~bands = ProbeBandAnalyzer(s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, smooth: 0.7);
)

// Adjust smoothing to eliminate transient blinking (0.0 = raw, 0.9 = ultra-smooth)
~bands.smooth = 0.85;

x.free;
~bands.close;
::

subsection:: 10. ProbeSpectralDashboard (4-Preset Spectral Workstation)
link::Classes/ProbeSpectralDashboard:: integrates multiple analysis tools into 4 synchronized presets:

code::
(
x = {
    var freq = LFNoise0.kr(4).exprange(150, 1200);
    Pulse.ar(freq, 0.5, 0.2).dup;
}.play;

~sdash = ProbeSpectralDashboard(s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite);
)

// Select presets programmatically:
~sdash.preset = \overview;   // FFT + 16-Bands + Descriptors
~sdash.preset = \pitch;      // Pitch tracker + Chromagram + FFT
~sdash.preset = \timeFreq;   // Spectrogram + 16-Band Analyzer
~sdash.preset = \compare;    // Dual-channel spectral comparison

x.free;
~sdash.close;
::

subsection:: 11. ProbeDashboard (5-Panel Master Command Center)
link::Classes/ProbeDashboard:: consolidates Meter, Scope, Spectrum, Spectrogram, and Loudness into a single window:

code::
s.dashboardPb(theme: \graphite);
::

subsection:: 12. ProbeInspector (Static Signal-Flow DAG Inspector)
link::Classes/ProbeInspector:: parses a SynthDef or running Synth into an interactive signal flow graph:

code::
(
SynthDef(\mySynth, { |out=0, freq=440, gate=1|
    var osc = Saw.ar(freq);
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.adsr(0.01, 0.2, 0.7, 0.5), gate);
    var filt = MoogFF.ar(osc, freq * 2, 2.5);
    Out.ar(out, (filt * env).dup);
}).add;
)

// Inspect SynthDef directly without running any audio
ProbeInspector(\mySynth, theme: \graphite);
::

subsection:: 13. ProbeHistory (Strip-Chart Timeline Recorder)
link::Classes/ProbeHistory:: logs audio dynamics over time:

code::
(
x = {
    var lfo = LFNoise2.kr(1).exprange(0.01, 0.5);
    (PinkNoise.ar(lfo)).dup;
}.play;

~hist = ProbeHistory(s, busIndex: 0, numChannels: 2, duration: 10, theme: \graphite);
)

x.free;
~hist.close;
::

subsection:: 14. ProbeTheme (Laboratory Aesthetics & Scaling)
link::Classes/ProbeTheme:: manages palettes and responsive font scaling:

code::
// Available themes: \graphite, \phosphor, \amber, \ice, \puredata
ProbeTheme.current = ProbeTheme.get(\puredata);

// Adjust font scale globally (1.0 = standard, 1.25 = default Retina, 1.5 = high visibility)
ProbeTheme.current = ProbeTheme.current.withFontScale(1.3);
::

section:: In-Graph Signal Tracing (.trace)

The code::.trace:: extension method (defined on link::Classes/UGen:: and link::Classes/Array::) allows instantaneous, zero-latency visual inspection of arbitrary internal nodes in a synthesis graph without altering signal flow, phase, or audio output.

subsection:: Syntax & Parameters
code::
aUGen.trace(label, mode, theme, options)
anArray.trace(label, mode, theme, options)
::
list::
## strong::label::: Optional String or Symbol for the window title and HUD readout.
## strong::mode::: Visualization mode:
list::
### code::\scope::: (default for audio-rate signals) High-speed oscilloscope using private bus and ScopeOut2.
### code::\history::: (default for control-rate signals) Numerical rolling HUD tracking values at 20 Hz.
### code::\spectrum::: FFT spectrum analyzer attached directly to the internal signal.
### code::\meter::: Vertical peak/RMS level meter.
::
## strong::theme::: Optional visual theme symbol (e.g. code::\graphite::, code::\phosphor::, code::\amber::, code::\ice::, code::\puredata::).
## strong::options::: Event dictionary for fine-tuning, e.g. code::(updateFreq: 30)::.
::

subsection:: Examples for Filters
Tracing filter cutoff modulation, pre-filter vs post-filter waveforms, and resonance:

code::
// 1. Resonant Lowpass Filter: Pre vs Post Filter & Cutoff Modulation
(
x = {
    var lfo = SinOsc.kr(0.5).exprange(150, 3500).trace("Cutoff LFO", \history);
    var raw = Saw.ar(110, 0.2).trace("Raw Saw Wave", \scope);
    var filtered = RLPF.ar(raw, lfo, 0.1).trace("RLPF Output", \scope);
    filtered.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Ladder Filter (MoogFF) Saturation & Resonance
(
x = {
    var osc = Pulse.ar(65, 0.3, 0.25).trace("Oscillator", \scope);
    var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.perc(0.05, 1.2), Dust.kr(1)).trace("Filter Env", \history);
    var cutoff = (env * 4000) + 100;
    var moog = MoogFF.ar(osc, cutoff, 3.2).trace("MoogFF Output", \scope, theme: \amber);
    moog.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Bandpass Resonance Sweep Traced via FFT Spectrum
(
x = {
    var sweep = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(300, 5000).trace("Sweep Hz", \history);
    var noise = WhiteNoise.ar(0.15);
    var bpf = BPF.ar(noise, sweep, 0.08).trace("Resonant Peak", \spectrum, theme: \phosphor);
    bpf.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::

subsection:: Examples for Analytic UGens
Tracing pitch trackers, envelope followers, spectral analyzers, and quadrature signals:

code::
// 1. Pitch Follower (Pitch.kr) Analysis
(
x = {
    var in = SinOsc.ar(LFNoise0.kr(2).exprange(200, 800), 0, 0.2);
    var pitchData = Pitch.kr(in);
    var freq = pitchData[0];
    var hasFreq = pitchData[1];
    
    // Trace audio signal in scope, detected frequency in timeline HUD
    in.trace("Audio In", \scope);
    freq.trace("Tracked Hz", \history);
    hasFreq.trace("Pitch Confidence (0/1)", \history);
    
    in.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Dynamic Envelope Follower (Amplitude.kr & PeakFollower.kr)
(
x = {
    var audio = Dust2.ar(8) * LFNoise1.kr(2).range(0.1, 0.8);
    var env = Amplitude.kr(audio, attackTime: 0.01, releaseTime: 0.1).trace("RMS Envelope", \history);
    var peak = PeakFollower.kr(audio, 0.999).trace("Peak Hold", \history);
    audio.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Spectral Feature Analytics (SpecCentroid & SpecFlatness)
(
x = {
    var sig = Saw.ar(XLine.kr(100, 3000, 5), 0.2);
    var chain = FFT(LocalBuf(2048), sig);
    var centroid = SpecCentroid.kr(chain).trace("Spectral Centroid (Hz)", \history);
    var flatness = SpecFlatness.kr(chain).trace("Spectral Flatness", \history);
    sig.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 4. Analytic Signal & Hilbert Transform (Quadrature 90-degree Phase Shift)
(
x = {
    var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.3);
    var quadrature = Hilbert.ar(sig); // [real, imag]
    quadrature.trace("Hilbert Quadrature", \scope, theme: \ice);
    quadrature;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::

subsection:: Examples for Modulation & Spatialization
code::
// 1. FM Synthesis Carrier and Modulator Traces
(
x = {
    var mod = SinOsc.ar(110, 0, 400).trace("Modulator", \scope);
    var car = SinOsc.ar(220 + mod, 0, 0.2).trace("FM Carrier", \scope);
    car.dup;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Stereo Panning & Spatial Rotation
(
x = {
    var sig = Pulse.ar(150, 0.5, 0.2);
    var panLfo = SinOsc.kr(0.4).trace("Pan Position", \history);
    var stereo = Pan2.ar(sig, panLfo).trace("Stereo Output", \scope);
    stereo;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::

section:: Embedding Probe Visualizers into Custom GUIs & Default SC GUI

Every instrument in the Probe suite provides an embeddable view factory constructor:
code::
Probe<Instrument>.view(parent, bounds, server, ...)
::
This returns the underlying embeddable view (a subclass of code::View::) which can be placed directly inside any custom code::Window::, code::CompositeView::, code::ScrollView::, code::VLayout::, or code::HLayout:: alongside stock SuperCollider widgets (code::Slider::, code::Knob::, code::Button::, code::NumberBox::, etc.).

subsection:: Example A: Complete Synthesizer Control Panel with Embedded Scope & Meter
This example demonstrates a complete synthesizer GUI window containing native SuperCollider sliders and buttons alongside embedded Probe visualizers:

code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var win, synth, freqSlider, resSlider, gateBtn;
    var scopeView, meterView;
    var synthDef;

    // 1. Define interactive synth
    synthDef = SynthDef(\probeGuiDemo, { |out=0, freq=220, res=0.2, gate=1|
        var osc = Mix([Saw.ar(freq * [0.99, 1.01]), Pulse.ar(freq * 0.5, 0.3)]) * 0.2;
        var env = EnvGen.kr(Env.adsr(0.02, 0.3, 0.6, 0.8), gate, doneAction: 0);
        var filt = RLPF.ar(osc, (freq * 4).clip(60, 16000), res);
        Out.ar(out, (filt * env).dup);
    }).add;

    s.sync;

    // 2. Create custom parent Window
    win = Window("Synth Channel Strip — Probe Embedded GUI", Rect(150, 150, 720, 380));
    win.view.background = Color.gray(0.12);

    // 3. Embed Probe Meter (left column)
    meterView = ProbeMeter.view(win, Rect(15, 20, 70, 340), s, numIns: 0, numOuts: 2, theme: \graphite);

    // 4. Embed Probe Scope (center antialiased oscilloscope)
    scopeView = ProbeScope.view(win, Rect(100, 20, 360, 220), s, busIndex: 0, numChannels: 2,
        theme: \graphite, engine: \smooth, style: \tracks);

    // 5. Native SuperCollider Controls (right column & bottom)
    // Frequency Slider
    StaticText(win, Rect(480, 20, 120, 20))
        .string_("Cutoff / Freq")
        .stringColor_(Color.white)
        .font_(Font("Helvetica", 11, true));

    freqSlider = Slider(win, Rect(480, 45, 210, 24))
        .value_(0.3)
        .action_({ |sl|
            var f = sl.value.linexp(0, 1, 60, 1200);
            if (synth.notNil) { synth.set(\freq, f) };
        });

    // Resonance Slider
    StaticText(win, Rect(480, 85, 120, 20))
        .string_("Filter Resonance")
        .stringColor_(Color.white)
        .font_(Font("Helvetica", 11, true));

    resSlider = Slider(win, Rect(480, 110, 210, 24))
        .value_(0.5)
        .action_({ |sl|
            var r = sl.value.linlin(0, 1, 0.05, 0.95);
            if (synth.notNil) { synth.set(\res, r) };
        });

    // Gate Toggle Button
    gateBtn = Button(win, Rect(480, 160, 100, 32))
        .states_([["Note ON", Color.white, Color.gray(0.25)], ["Note OFF", Color.black, Color.green(0.8)]])
        .action_({ |btn|
            if (btn.value == 1) {
                synth = Synth(\probeGuiDemo, [\freq, freqSlider.value.linexp(0, 1, 60, 1200), \res, resSlider.value.linlin(0, 1, 0.05, 0.95)]);
            } {
                if (synth.notNil) { synth.set(\gate, 0); synth = nil; };
            };
        });

    // Theme Selector Menu for embedded views
    PopUpMenu(win, Rect(480, 210, 130, 24))
        .items_(["Graphite", "Phosphor", "Amber", "Ice", "PureData"])
        .action_({ |menu|
            var thName = [\graphite, \phosphor, \amber, \ice, \puredata][menu.value];
            var newTheme = ProbeTheme.get(thName);
            meterView.theme = newTheme;
            scopeView.theme = newTheme;
        });

    // Cleanup on window close
    win.onClose = {
        if (synth.notNil) { synth.free };
        meterView.stop;
        scopeView.stop;
    };

    win.front;
});
)
::

subsection:: Example B: Mastering Monitoring Console (Loudness + Vectorscope + Band Analyzer)
This example demonstrates a multi-instrument mastering panel combining loudness, stereo phase, and ISO 1/3-octave frequency distribution in a single window using SuperCollider's layout managers:

code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var win, lufsView, vecView, bandView;
    var sound;

    // Test stereo signal
    sound = {
        var bass = SinOsc.ar(55) * 0.4;
        var lead = Saw.ar([220, 222]) * 0.15;
        var noise = PinkNoise.ar(0.05);
        (bass + lead + noise);
    }.play;

    win = Window("Mastering & Quality Control Console", Rect(100, 100, 840, 360));
    win.view.background = Color.gray(0.1);

    // Embed instruments side-by-side using exact Rect bounds
    lufsView = ProbeLoudness.view(win, Rect(15, 15, 200, 330), s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, target: \streaming);
    vecView  = ProbeVectorscope.view(win, Rect(225, 15, 260, 330), s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, engine: \smooth);
    bandView = ProbeBandAnalyzer.view(win, Rect(495, 15, 330, 330), s, busIndex: 0, theme: \graphite, smooth: 0.7);

    win.onClose = {
        sound.free;
        lufsView.stop;
        vecView.stop;
        bandView.stop;
    };

    win.front;
});
)
::

subsection:: Example C: Embedding Alongside Default SuperCollider GUI Windows
You can embed any Probe view into standard SuperCollider container views, such as alongside a code::ServerMeterView:: or inside a custom status panel:

code::
(
s.waitForBoot({
    var win = Window("Server Status & Precision Scope", Rect(200, 200, 520, 280));
    var meter, scope;

    // Embed Probe antialiased oscilloscope
    scope = ProbeScope.view(win, Rect(10, 10, 360, 250), s, busIndex: 0, numChannels: 2, theme: \phosphor, engine: \smooth);

    // Embed stock ServerMeterView alongside ProbeScope
    meter = ServerMeterView(s, win, Rect(380, 10, 130, 250), 2, 2);

    win.onClose = {
        scope.stop;
    };

    win.front;
});
)
::

section:: Key Invariants & Best Practices

numberedlist::
## strong::Audio-Thread Safety::: None of the Probe visualizers allocate memory or execute blocking system calls on the real-time audio thread. Shared-memory ScopeBuffers and circular RecordBuf allocations execute on the server command thread.
## strong::Resource Reclamation::: Always call code::view.stop:: or close parent windows when finished. Probe views register with code::ServerTree:: and code::ServerQuit:: to automatically clean up synthetic resources upon server reboot or cmd-period.
## strong::Smooth vs Native Engine Selection::: Use strong::\smooth:: (default) for pristine, sub-pixel antialiased waveforms with configurable thickness on Retina displays. Use strong::\native:: when zero SCLang vector draw overhead is required on low-powered machines.
## strong::Zero Core SC Overrides::: Probe never alters code::s.meter::, code::s.scope::, or code::s.freqscope::. Use code::s.*Pb:: or the high-level class constructors.
::
